  },
  "fintro": {
   "fill": "green",
   "page": "flows",
   "text": "Every screen of the Clean prototype, grouped by flow and read left to right. Each frame is the live prototype opened on that exact state. Numbers match the list beside each row.",
   "w": 480,
   "x": -560,
   "y": -260
  },
  "fn0": {
   "fill": "gray",
   "maxH": 875,
   "page": "flows",
   "text": "Home is the starting point. PayPal AI opens beside the rail, not over the page, and answers with sources and next steps.\n\n1. Home\n2. Open PayPal AI · starter prompts\n3. Ask · answer with sources and actions",
   "w": 480,
   "x": -560,
   "y": 0
  },
  "fn1": {
   "fill": "gray",
   "maxH": 875,
   "page": "flows",
   "text": "Move money in from the balance card. A sheet picks the amount; a toast confirms, the balance updates, and the top up is recorded in Transactions as a positive inflow.\n\n1. Home · balance card\n2. Add money to PayPal\n3. Added · toast and new balance\n4. Recorded in Transactions · inflow",
   "w": 480,
   "x": -560,
   "y": 1400
  },
  "fn10": {
   "fill": "gray",
   "maxH": 875,
   "page": "flows",
   "text": "The AI panel stays open beside whichever page the user is on, so answers can point at what is on screen.\n\n1. Dining · on Transactions\n2. What’s due · on Recurring\n3. Reorder · on Essentials\n4. Can I afford… · on Wallet\n5. Cancel · on Recurring",
   "w": 480,
   "x": -560,
   "y": 14000
  },
  "fn11": {
   "fill": "gray",
   "maxH": 875,
   "page": "flows",
   "text": "The avatar at the bottom of the rail opens Settings: profile details, security, notification and PayPal AI preferences.\n\n1. Settings",
   "w": 480,
   "x": -560,
   "y": 15400
  },
  "fn12": {
   "fill": "gray",
   "maxH": 875,
   "page": "flows",
   "text": "Budget is a rail page with two sections, Essentials and Spending: editable amounts, an Add category button under each, and an x to remove a row (with a confirm dialog). A summary ring shows what is left. PayPal AI can suggest limits in chat or on the page; nothing changes until the user applies it.\n\n1. Budget\n2. AI suggestions\n3. Suggest in chat\n4. Applied\n5. Add a category\n6. Remove a category\n7. Category details",
   "w": 480,
   "x": -560,
   "y": 16800
  },
  "fn2": {
   "fill": "gray",
   "maxH": 875,
   "page": "flows",
   "text": "Find, filter and understand any transaction. Charges PayPal AI can’t categorise get a review prompt.\n\n1. Transactions · chart and list\n2. Category filter menu\n3. Filtered to Dining\n4. Transaction details panel\n5. Change category · picker\n6. Category saved · toast\n7. Needs-review charge\n8. Page 2 of results",
   "w": 480,
   "x": -560,
   "y": 2800
  },
  "fn3": {
   "fill": "gray",
   "maxH": 875,
   "page": "flows",
   "text": "PayPal AI’s agent (Kernel) cancels in a secure cloud browser, only after the user approves, and leaves proof and an undo.\n\n1. Recurring · subscriptions and bills\n2. Subscription details panel\n3. Confirm cancellation\n4. Kernel run · live browser and steps\n5. Cancelled · toast with Undo\n6. Cancelled state · proof",
   "w": 480,
   "x": -560,
   "y": 4200
  },
  "fn4": {
   "fill": "gray",
   "maxH": 875,
   "page": "flows",
   "text": "See what is due by day, and inspect a bill (bills are tracked, never suggested for cancelling).\n\n1. Payment calendar · day selected\n2. Bill details panel",
   "w": 480,
   "x": -560,
   "y": 5600
  },
  "fn5": {
   "fill": "gray",
   "maxH": 875,
   "page": "flows",
   "text": "Select household items, review the order, and let the checkout agent place it with the partner store.\n\n1. Essentials · items\n2. Review order\n3. Placing the order · steps\n4. Order placed\n5. Order history · Buy again",
   "w": 480,
   "x": -560,
   "y": 7000
  },
  "fn6": {
   "fill": "gray",
   "maxH": 875,
   "page": "flows",
   "text": "Add a cash-back offer, pay with PayPal, receive cash back in 3–5 days.\n\n1. Offers gallery\n2. Offer details panel\n3. Offer added",
   "w": 480,
   "x": -560,
   "y": 8400
  },
  "fn7": {
   "fill": "gray",
   "maxH": 875,
   "page": "flows",
   "text": "Check points, redeem them to balance (recorded in Transactions as an inflow), and choose the monthly 5% category.\n\n1. Rewards\n2. Redeem points\n3. 5% category chosen\n4. Redemption recorded in Transactions",
   "w": 480,
   "x": -560,
   "y": 9800
  },
  "fn8": {
   "fill": "gray",
   "maxH": 875,
